     rrccssmmeerrggee — merge RCS revisions

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rrccssmmeerrggee [--EEVV] [--kk_m_o_d_e] [--pp[_r_e_v]] [--qq[_r_e_v]] [--xx_s_u_f_f_i_x_e_s] [--zz_t_z] --rr_r_e_v
              _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrccssmmeerrggee program merges changes between two revisions of an RCS file
     into the corresponding working file.

     rrccssmmeerrggee also supports keyword substitution – see the rcs(1) man page for
     more information.

     The following options are supported:

     --EE      Default merge: see diff3(1) for details.

     --kk_m_o_d_e  Specify the keyword substitution mode.

     --pp[_r_e_v]
             Print result to standard output.

     --qq[_r_e_v]
             Be quiet about reporting.

     --rr_r_e_v   Merge with respect to revision _r_e_v.  This option should be speci‐
             fied twice to merge changes between two specific revisions.  If
             only one revision is specified, merging is done between that re‐
             vision and the latest revision of the default branch.

     --VV      Print RCS's version number.

     --xx_s_u_f_f_i_x_e_s
             Specify the suffixes for RCS files.  Suffixes should be separated
             by the ‘/’ character.

     --zz_t_z    Specify the time zone for keyword substitution.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     RCSINIT  If set, this variable should contain a list of space-delimited
              options that are prepended to the argument list.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The rrccssmmeerrggee utility exits with one of the following values:

           0       No overlaps.
           1       Overlaps were found.
           2       An error occurred.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Merge differences between revision 1.4 and 1.8 of _f_o_o_._c and print the re‐
     sult to standard output:

           $ rcsmerge -p -r1.4 -r1.8 foo.c

     Undo changes between revision 2.4 and 2.8 of _f_o_o_._c, overwriting the work‐
     ing copy:

           $ rcsmerge -r2.8 -r2.4 foo.c

